<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rudolf Diesel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1858–1913</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rudolf Diesel was a German engineer who invented the diesel engine, a compression-ignition engine far more efficient than the steam engines of his day. He patented the design in 1892–1893 and built working engines with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augsburg">Augsburg</a> engineering works, later part of MAN, between 1893 and 1897. He disappeared from a steamer crossing to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> in 1913.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rudolf-diesel.jpg" alt="Rudolf Diesel" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rudolf_Diesel2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
